WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.340
Process creation is security-relevant because launching another program crosses a boundary between the parent process and a new execution context.

2
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:19.800
The child may inherit privileges, environment variables, working directory assumptions, open descriptors or handles, resource access, and operational context from the parent.

3
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:31.520
A child process can influence files, logs, network connections, temporary storage, resource consumption, and later decisions made by the parent or by surrounding automation.

4
00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.820
Its exit status may decide whether a workflow continues.

5
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.560
Its output may be parsed by another component.

6
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.020
Its side effects may persist after the parent has moved on.

7
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:46.900
Unsafe launch behavior often comes from hidden assumptions rather than one dramatic mistake.

8
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:59.240
The code may assume the intended program was selected, that arguments are only data, that the shell is not involved, that the environment is harmless, or that open resources will not be inherited.

9
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.980
Each assumption should be made explicit.

10
00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:05.460
Responsible process creation starts with a contract.

11
00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.320
Which program is launched?

12
00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.660
How is the program path chosen?

13
00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:11.360
How are arguments represented?

14
00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.100
What environment and working directory are used?

15
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.080
Which descriptors or handles are inherited?

16
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:19.660
Which identity and resource limits apply?

17
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.680
How are errors, output, and timeouts handled?

18
00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:28.280
This course treats process launch as an engineering workflow.

19
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:33.020
The goal is not fear of child processes; it is intentional design.

20
00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:44.080
A maintainable launcher selects programs explicitly, passes structured arguments, constrains inherited state, manages the lifecycle, and gives reviewers a clear set of decisions to verify.
